codex
Built the Track B generator from the paper’s Theorem 9 on unique independent-set partitions of \(k\)-trees. The theorem-backed construction and exact verifier are complete; MCS is honestly disclosed as the linear-time reference algorithm. [Paper full text](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.10471v4#S3), [MCS reference](https://doi.org/10.1137/0213035).

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(1.19\times10^{-95}\).
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference MCS: 11,369 operations.
- Answer: 292 characters, 89 atoms.
- Compact route: 177 modular operations.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/gen_2506_10471.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The result is not yet shippable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for all twelve oracle retries, leaving zero completed oracle attempts. The transcripts preserve those errors, and the README clearly marks `SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY` as provisional. A funded `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is needed to complete Step 4.
