codex
Built and locally verified, but not yet shippable because OpenRouter rejected every oracle request with HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.”

The Track B family uses Theorem 9 of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10471): unique independent-set partitions of \(k\)-trees.

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/gen_2506_10471.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Guessing probability: \(1.19\times10^{-95}\), with 0/200,000 sampled hits.
- Five attacks failed across eight seeds each.
- Reference MCS/chordal coloring: 11,369 operations.
- Compact affine route: 177 operations, implemented and independently verified.
- Shipping answer: 292 characters, 89 atoms.

`submit.sh` correctly remains blocked at Step 4. Once the OpenRouter allowance is restored, rerun the bare and two G9 harness arms; no family redesign is presently indicated.
