codex
I caught and corrected a genuine G4 flaw before shipping: the first decoy design used degree-three vertices, which a solver can exclude for free, so sampling them overstated the answer space. I’m replacing each distractor with a degree-four face-stacking center plus a degree-three satellite. The structure-aware sampler excludes only the satellites and samples uniformly from all degree-eligible vertices; rejecting the degree-four centers now requires the actual local octahedron test. This preserves a fixed 240-atom answer while enlarging the honest haystack.
apply patch
