codex
Built a native Track B generator from the paper’s Section 8 octahedral decomposition ([arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10471)).

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Exact valid-answer count at shipping: 1.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference Algorithm X method: 8/8, 146,204 counted operations.
- Answer: 996 characters, 240 atoms.
- Canonical-key invariance: 20/20.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/gen_2506_10471.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The remaining blocker is external: every hardening call returned HTTP 403, “Key limit exceeded (total limit).” Consequently, the transcripts contain only errors and provide no oracle-hardness evidence. This is documented prominently in the README; no rejection was written and no results were fabricated. Once OpenRouter quota is restored, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.10471
